# --- secrets -----------------------------------------------------------
# The real config carries Discord/Slack/Telegram webhooks and bot tokens.
# Only config.example.json (every field blank) belongs in the repo.
config.json

# --- captured data -----------------------------------------------------
# data/ IS tracked. The SQLite history is the backtest material, and the
# cached RHP/anchor zips are what make a backtest reproducible: the engine
# re-downloads them from exchange URLs that rot, so a clone six months from
# now would silently analyse a different (or empty) document set.
# Only the transient SQLite sidecars are excluded - they are rebuilt on open
# and committing them risks shipping a half-applied transaction.
data/*.db-shm
data/*.db-wal
data/*.db-journal

# --- generated output --------------------------------------------------
# reports/ and briefings/ ARE tracked, as worked examples of what the engine
# produces. Note that reports/index.md and the memo PDF contain the capital
# figure from config (total_capital) and the resulting deployment plan.
# Root-anchored: the release archives live here. NOT data/documents/*.zip,
# which is tracked cache, so this must never become a bare `*.zip`.
/*.zip

# --- python ------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

# --- macOS -------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
